From 31933118366d90c95cbfaa1466136adef8546ac4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:36:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 077/108] gpu: vulkan: lazy resolve dumps; depth resolves also
 feed k_8_8_8_8 textures

A 1x k_8_8_8_8 resolve that feeds a texture (vulkan_resolve_feed_textures) no
longer writes guest memory at once (vulkan_resolve_feed_lazy_dump, default on):
the write is recorded when something requests that memory - a SharedMemory
RangeRequestListener hook at the start of RequestRanges (texture loads, vertex
data, memexport) - by the direct resolve compute shader reading the fed texture
through a view undoing the red/blue swap, with the resolve's own EDRAM base and
pitch so the source pixel is the texture pixel. Dumps a later resolve
overwrites completely are dropped; partial overlaps are written first. Fed
textures with pending dumps are not evicted. Lightning Returns field: 12
deferred, 0 written per frame; the ten 1280x720 resolves 1.81 -> 0.72 ms.

A kD24S8 depth resolve now also feeds a k_8_8_8_8 texture at the destination
(the raw depth/stencil word, red/blue swapped like the copy shader does for
format 0) besides the k_24_8 one: the game samples the resolved depth both
ways. Removes two 1280x720 texture loads per frame (0.66 ms) for ~0.2 ms of
feed draws.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

